# English UI label casing

For **en** strings that are buttons, primary actions, nav items, page titles, or modal titles: use **Title Case** — capitalise every principal word, including the second word.

## Do

- `Add Bay`, `Add Bays`, `Add Vendor`, `New Job Card`, `Save Changes`
- `Parts Requests`, `Purchase Orders`, `Vendor Bills`

## Do not

- `Add bay`, `Add bays`, `Add vendor`, `New job card`, `Save changes` (as a button/title)

## Applies to

- `messages/en.json` keys used as buttons, nav, page headers, dialog titles
- Default trigger / primary button copy in components

## Does not apply to

- Full sentences, hints, empty-state body copy, or validation messages (those stay sentence case)
- `hi.json` / `gu.json` (follow normal language rules; do not force English Title Case)

When adding or changing English UI labels, match vendors-style Title Case (`Add Vendor`) — never leave the second word lowercase in an action name.
